KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp23 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ print returned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  With the libstdc++ 16 headers, CBMC does not finish
within 300 s (the test has no unwinding bound; symbolic execution of
std::vprint_unicode's formatting into a buffer and the unicode check does not
end).  The program has no observable result but its termination.
